WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know
our first guest tonight

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
from films like "300"
and "Olympus Has Fallen."

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.840
He stars in "Hunter Killer,"
which is in theaters Friday.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.008 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.410 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-75! 50 feet!

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
40 feet!
-Cast it!

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.014 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-30 feet! 2-5!

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Terminal holding, Captain.
-Right full rudder.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right full rudder,
aye, Captain.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.197 line:92%
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
our friend Gerard Butler,
everybody.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:36.569 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:46.312 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Welcome back.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.226 line:92%
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.061 line:92%
I think you're living the dream.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.563
I feel like, if you're an actor
who at some point in your career

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:08.068
gets to scream "right full
rudder," that's the dream.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.503 size:78% position:39%
-I actually had a --
I was in a Bond movie

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
right at the beginning
of my career,

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.507 line:92%
and I got to say things like --

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.310 line:92%
I was a sailor on a ship saying,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Torpedoes bearing range,
6,000."

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:20.780 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And while I'm filming,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.816 size:81% position:41%
the quartermaster said
he wouldn't say that.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it all got taken away
from me.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, he took away your lines.
-He took away my lines.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.555
And I was left with,
"We're down by the stern, sir."

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:33.159
So from that day, I said,
"I am making a submarine movie.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:33.927 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm going to produce it

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
and nobody is going to take
my lines away."

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:37.430 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There you go.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play a captain
in this movie.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.433 line:92%
And there's a coup in Russia.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're sort of preventing
a world war.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.938 line:92%
Normal stuff for Gerard Butler.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:45.772 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Normal stuff. Yeah.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.307 line:92%
-A regular day at the office.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.341 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But this is interesting.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.776 line:92%
The Pentagon, the Navy asked you

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
to actually
give a press conference

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.480 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to talk about the film.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.247 line:92%
And this is a real thing.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.182
You went and gave a press
conference at the Pentagon.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.718
And I should point out --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.122 line:92%
Like, you're -- so this --

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to make sure
everybody knows.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're an actor
talking about a movie.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
But these are real reporters.
Right?

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Yes.
-How was it?

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:12.031
-Unfortunately they put in the
real reporters, not fake ones.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:12.565 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:16.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so the Navy were
incredible in supporting us

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.738
with this movie, and then I was
invited to the Pentagon.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought,
"Great, I'm going to go along,

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.641 line:92%
get a trip around the Pentagon

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're going to
show me around."

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said, "And if you can
just do a press conference

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:26.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the end."

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they gave me information
about the Navy.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm thinking -- I'm more
defending them, saying,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't worry, you didn't spend
any money,

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
necessarily deviate
from their missions."

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.256 line:92%
And as we get there, I look out,

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.925
and I go,
"I recognize this room, though."

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I walk out and I look
behind me and I'm --

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.730 line:92%
That's the Pentagon sign.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.964 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm actually doing a --

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.399 line:92%
and I see Barbara Starr of CNN

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:49.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the first question
is Saudi Arabia.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:49.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, boy.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.071
-The second question is, "How do
you solve Saudi Arabia?"

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:56.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Okay, I don't know.
Did we get the same memo?"

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:56.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, I didn't --
[ Applause ]

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.113 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And it was 32 minutes.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-32 minutes at the Pentagon.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I still didn't quite
appreciate it until afterwards

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.755
when I saw photos and it's me
standing in front of the panel.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:12.492
I know that sounds stupid, but I
really didn't appreciate it

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.760 line:92%
until I see the photos and go,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, I was actually doing
a press conference."

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just like to think of
an editor saying,

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:19.399 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Who gave these quotes?"

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like,
"It was Gerard Butler today."

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:23.937 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, yeah.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was even
a headline saying --

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:25.872 line:92%
I saw it after, but it said,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:29.709
"Gerard Butler speaks live from
the Pentagon in a few minutes."

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:33.279
And you go, "That's -- I see
that with Trump, I see that,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.714 line:92%
but Gerard Butler speaks live"?

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.715 line:92%
Like, what's he got to say?

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say, like,
five years ago,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
that crawl on CNN
I would think is weird.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now anything, I'm like,
whatever.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:41.921 line:92%
-That's true. That's true.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's not crazier
than anything else.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:44.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.492 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Did you actually go --

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.262
You went out on a submarine
just to do a little research.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.531
-Yeah. I went out with the
director, Donovan Marsh.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
Went out on this --
it was one of the most,

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.635
maybe the most incredible
experiences I ever had

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:59.005
going out for three days
underway from Pearl Harbor.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:02.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we did all the maneuvers
that we do in the movie.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
So battle stations
and deep dives

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.778 line:92%
and fire drills, et cetera.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.113 line:92%
But when we first went out --

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the drills
they do is man overboard.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.583 line:92%
But they do man overboard.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.653
They're not going to throw a man
overboard every time,

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.954 line:92%
so they throw a bag of popcorn.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right.
-Into the ocean, right?

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's far more disposable.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they spend
the next four minutes

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to rescue this popcorn
from the ocean.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:24.464 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
This 8,000-ton sub that stops,
maneuvers back, forward,

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.801
and then somebody climbs out of
the hatch

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
and dives into the water
and grabs the popcorn

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.438 line:92%
before, hopefully, it bursts.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like if a boat
was going by and saw that,

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:37.543
they would just think, "I can't
believe that's the only popcorn

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have on that submarine."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.483 line:92%
-Yeah, we did eat that popcorn.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:47.487
Yeah, we dried it out in the
microwave and then we had it.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:51.591
And then the captain also lit up
a cigar before we went out.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:54.460
He was like, "Okay, this is
what we're going to do."

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.295 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So we lit up a cigar.

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.429 line:92%
I'm thinking, "This is insane."

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm on top of
a hunter killer submarine

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:01.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
and feeling a bit queasy,
though, and all I hear is --

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:01.734 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Grunting ]

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I turn around and I'm
looking at the captain, like,

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:05.438 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Is that Donovan?"

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Donovan is over the back,
throwing up.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.243 size:84% position:42%
-That's your director?
-Our director, Donovan,

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
is throwing up
on the edge of the tower.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:16.516 line:92%
Gone was that hope that we could

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
pretend to be
bad-ass movie people.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say you played right
into the stereotype

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.057 line:92%
that the Navy had of you, yeah.

